# Testing

- Every new or changed business rule requires a focused automated test.
- Unit-test entities and value objects with deterministic inputs.
- Test use cases using fakes or stubs for their ports; do not instantiate real infrastructure.
- Integration-test Drizzle adapters, PostgreSQL constraints, mappings, and transactions that protect behavior.
- Add Playwright coverage for critical end-to-end flows when the harness exists.
- Structure tests visibly as Arrange–Act–Assert or Given–When–Then.
- A bug fix should include a regression test when reasonable.
- Test useful behavior and boundaries, not merely that a class can be instantiated.
- Keep test data free of real personal or sensitive information.

Do not weaken production types or visibility only to make testing easier.
